<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Atar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Atar is a town in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a> and the capital of the Adrar region. An oasis of date palms on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a> across the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>, it became the main centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Adrar. French forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-gouraud">Henri Gouraud</a> occupied it in 1909, and today it is the gateway for travel to the old towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinguetti">Chinguetti</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ouadane">Ouadane</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/atar.jpg" alt="Atar" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:LouisAragon (uploader) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_coin_of_Ardashir_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
